Audit anything still using getxattr/setxattr interfaces with XATTR_NAME_FSCAPS.
 - evm just seems to calculate hmac on the raw xattr data, so it should be okay.

Check overlayfs copy-up of fscaps. Seems likely this needs to be updated to use
{get,set}_fscaps.

Look at cap_inode_setxattr(). It skips check for XATTR_NAME_CAPS. Should this stay?
It's a little unclear, but probably. vfs_setxattr() will no longer set fscaps, but
__vfs_setxattr_locked() will and changing cap_inode_setxattr() behavior would
affect how it behaves. So far the assumption has been that callers of the lower-
level xattr functions should know what they are doing with fscaps.

This series doesn't touch removexattr(). I think this is fine, but should think a
bit more on it.

Look into whether vfs_caps_from_xattr() and get_vfs_caps_from_disk() need to be
seperate or if they can be combined into one function. Ditto with having two
rootid_owns_currentns() implementations.
